>Jove, why the scrolls of gold detection?  

  To find the Portals on the Elemental Planes.  They're not visible at
first.  You have to step through the portals exit the Planes, generally
while being mobbed on a wide open level by monsters a lot tougher than
the ones you'd been fighting in the Dungeons.  (See my ttyrec page for
examples.)

  Reading a non-cursed scroll of gold detection while confused is the
best way to find the portals on the Elemental Planes.

  For more see here:
<http://www.mindspring.com/~jove/Spoilers/Portal-343.txt>

>Also, I'm assuming the method
>of confusing yourself has to do with reading scrolls of enchant
>weapon/armor...  What is the difference between reading, while
>confused, a cursed scroll of destroy armor vs. an uncursed scroll of
>enchant armor?

  Confused reading of a cursed scroll of destroy armor will make a
semi-random piece of worn armor fire/rust/rot-proof.  It will *not* fix
rusted, corroded, rotted, burnt, etc armor.

  This can save having to read non-cursed scrolls of Enchant Armor while
confused to make armor fire/rust resistant.  Sometimes you'll find
scrolls of Destroy Armor.  Even if you don't they take fewer magic
marker charges to write than ?oEnchantArmor.  The marker charges saved
can be used to write more ?oEnchantArmor.

  Note that there's almost no other use for a ?oDestroyArmor (well, for
getting rid of worn cursed armor.  Better not to wear cursed armor in
the first place.)

  Reading a non-cursed scroll of enchant armor while confused will
semi-randomly fire/rust-proof one worn piece of armor.  If that piece of
armor was damaged it will be repaired.  This is generally a poor use of
scrolls of Enchant Armor.  Most armor can be easily replaced.  Most
armor also has a base AC of 1.  So repair gives an average of 1 more
point of AC.  A blessed scroll of Enchant Armor should average 2 more
points of AC.


